        "topicId": "math-y9-changing-subject",
        "stem": "A model has the form $y=a(x-h)^2+b$, with a>0. It produces y=21 at both x=−1 and x=5, and y=11 at x=4. Original inputs are restricted to −4≤x≤8. Which option gives all inverse branches for x in terms of y (retaining only inputs in the original domain) and the complete set S of inputs producing y=35?",
        "options": [
          {
            "latex": "x=2+\\sqrt{(y-3)/2};\\ S=\\{6\\}",
            "errorPath": "Keep positive branch only.",
            "id": "A"
          },
          {
            "latex": "x=2\\pm\\sqrt{(y-3)/2};\\ S=\\{-2,6\\}",
            "id": "B"
          },
          {
            "id": "C",
            "latex": "x=2\\pm\\sqrt{(y+3)/2};\\ S=\\{-2,6\\}",
            "errorPath": "Move offset 3 with the wrong sign in the inverse, but obtain the correct numerical set by checking the original calibrated model."
