            "errorPath": "Forget square root, giving x=−14 or18 outside domain.",
            "id": "E"
          },
          {
            "latex": "x=2\\pm\\sqrt{(y-3)/2};\\ S=\\{-2\\}",
            "errorPath": "Keep negative branch only.",
            "id": "F"
          }
        ],
        "correctOptionId": "B",
        "correctAnswerLatex": "x=2\\pm\\sqrt{(y-3)/2};\\ S=\\{-2,6\\}",
        "workedSolutionSteps": [
          "Equal outputs imply equal squared distances from h: h is midpoint of −1 and5, so h2.",
          "9a+b=21,4a+b=11, giving a2,b3. Thus x=2±√((y−3)/2), restricted to domain.",
          "At y35, square root4, giving −2 and6, both permitted."
        ],
